  "offline_independent_scope": [
    "Root inspected the actual ptrace lineage/root exec verification, fatal syscall policy, exact AF_UNIX anonymous IPC exception and IPv4/IPv6 probe disjoint binding; todo_acceptance independently ran the preserved parser/negative controls.",
    "The standalone host control baseline admits 0 to 1 filters only when inherited-parent enforcement is explicitly disabled for that control. Every actual product and protocol probe still requires inherited parent enforcement, same PID/NSpid and exactly one added fatal filter.",
    "No absence of observable trace is treated as zero traffic. Unknown remains null, killed child processes cannot be hidden by a successful parent, and failure diagnostic output never grants acceptance.",
    "The revised Rust spawn IPC exception admits only an 8-byte, flags-zero, address-NULL recvfrom after the complete product trace proves a unique anonymous reciprocal-peer AF_UNIX pair was created earlier in that tree; missing or ambiguous inode provenance rejects acceptance.",
    "pidfd_getfd and ancillary message operations remain denied, eliminating imported socket descriptors from the local IPC proof. Ordinary socket, connect, bind, send and io_uring remain denied. IPv4 and IPv6 must reach their exact-family attempted syscall and terminate with SIGSYS.",
    "Controlled Python launches use -I -S; the archived prior AF_UNIX probe failure has no call stack and is not assigned a proven Python site/NSS cause. New default and semantic fatal-network product gates have not yet executed."
  ],
